.\" Manual page for flyleaf.
.\"
.\" It exists because the binary takes an argument and has no --help to
.\" describe it: src/main.rs reads args_os().nth(1) and nothing else, so this
.\" is the only place that argument is written down. slipcase-desktop's page
.\" exists for the same reason, and lintian tagged its absence there.
.\"
.\" @VERSION@ is substituted by packaging/debian/build-deb.sh, the same way
.\" control.in is, so the version in the header cannot drift from the package.
.\" The date is the date this page was last revised and not the build date,
.\" which is the convention and is also what makes the page reproducible.
.\"
.\" Author: David M. Anderson
.\" Built with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic)
.TH FLYLEAF 1 "2026\-09\-07" "flyleaf @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flyleaf \- structure\-aware TOML editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flyleaf
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tommy Flyleaf
opens a TOML file and shows it as a tree beside what a save would write.
Values are edited by their type, keys, tables, arrays and comments can be
added, renamed, converted and removed, and a save keeps every comment, the
key order, the whitespace and the quoting of everything that was not edited.
.PP
It is a windowed application, normally started by opening a file from a file
manager rather than from a shell. The package registers the desktop entry
that makes that work, so a .toml file opens on a double\-click once the
application is chosen for it.
.SH OPTIONS
There are none.
.B flyleaf
is a window rather than a command\-line interface, and it takes one optional
positional argument and nothing else.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I file
The TOML file to open. With no argument the window opens empty and offers to
choose one.
.PP
A file that cannot be read, or is not TOML, is reported in the window rather
than on the standard error, with the line and column the parser objected to,
because the argument usually arrives from a file manager where nobody is
watching a terminal.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save. The file is written beside itself and renamed over the original, so a
failure at any point leaves the original whole.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Save as.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z
Undo and redo. Edits to one row are one step.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns success when the window has been closed. A non\-zero status means the
window could not be created at all \(em no display, or no usable graphics
driver \(em rather than anything about a file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/flyleaf.desktop
The desktop entry, naming application/toml.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg\-mime (1),
.BR update\-desktop\-database (1)
.PP
The TOML specification is at https://toml.io. The plan and the design
decisions behind this application are in DESIGN.md in its repository.
.SH AUTHOR
David M. Anderson
